# Training

- `training/` is **pure Python**: never built by colcon, never shipped in the car
  image. Run commands from the `training/` directory. See
  [training/README.md](training/README.md).
- The RL approach follows GT Sophy: QR-SAC in [training/qrsac/](training/qrsac/),
  the sim env in [training/f1tenth_env/](training/f1tenth_env/). Background:
  [docs/context.md](docs/context.md).
- The observation/action layout is the shared contract
  ([libs/f1tenth_contract](libs/f1tenth_contract/)), installed **editable** — a
  format change is picked up on the next run with no rebuild, but it also affects
  `racing_rl` and the C++ mirror, so treat it as a shared-surface change.
- No mocks — tests exercise the real env and modules. Run them where the training
  dependencies (e.g. Genesis) are actually installed, rather than faking or
  skipping them.
- Keep heavy artifacts (checkpoints, logs, wandb) out of git; they are gitignored.
